WEBVTT

00:05.680 --> 00:10.270
Remember how before we said this whole course was really just about relationships between numbers?

00:10.450 --> 00:13.630
Well, up to now, we've been talking mostly about fractions.

00:13.690 --> 00:18.880
And this is the point at which we're switching gears to talk about decimal numbers instead.

00:19.720 --> 00:24.340
The reason we're doing fractions in decimals back to back is because many numbers can be expressed as

00:24.340 --> 00:26.220
either a fraction or a decimal.

00:26.230 --> 00:30.760
So decimals are a different way to express the fractions we've already been learning about.

00:31.210 --> 00:36.700
For example, if you have 45 minutes to get where you're going, you can express that as a fraction

00:36.700 --> 00:44.800
as three over 4 hours or three fourths hours or as a decimal as 0.7 5 hours.

00:45.220 --> 00:50.350
Later in this section, we'll deal with some more advanced decimal concepts, but we'll start by talking

00:50.350 --> 00:56.320
about place value, which will give us some context about what specifically the seven means in a decimal

00:56.320 --> 01:01.120
like 0.75 compared to what specifically the five means.
